13:T40e,President Donald Trump, with a net worth of approximately $6 billion according to Forbes, owns a range of stocks across media, technology, and finance. His top holding is Trump Media & Technology Group Corp. (DJT), the parent company of Truth Social, valued at around $2 billion. Other notable investments include Blue Owl Capital Corp. (OBDC), Apple Inc. (AAPL), Microsoft Corp. (MSFT), Nvidia Corp. (NVDA), Blackstone Inc. (BX), Broadcom Inc. (AVGO), and Alphabet Inc. (GOOG, GOOGL). The stakes in these companies range from hundreds of thousands to millions of dollars, reflecting a diversified approach with exposure to tech giants and financial assets. Trump Media & Technology Group remains a significant personal investment, representing about 41.5% of the company. While Trump has filed to potentially sell some shares, he has stated he has no immediate plans to do so. His financial disclosures provide a window into the president’s investment strategy and focus on companies with strong market positions or dividend potential.4:[["$","$Lf",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"NewsArticle\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://www.pressorahub.com/investing/donald-trump-stock-portfolio-8-stocks-owned/\"},\"headline\":\"Donald Trump’s Stock Portfolio: 8 Stocks Owned by the President\",\"description\":\"A look at eight publicly disclosed stocks in President Donald Trump’s portfolio, including Trump Media, Apple, Microsoft, and Nvidia.\",\"image\":\"/images/trump-stock-portfolio.webp\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"David Miller\",\"url\":\"https://www.pressorahub.com/our-team/\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"PressoraHub\",\"logo\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"url\":\"https://www.pressorahub.com/images/pressorahub-logo.webp\"}},\"datePublished\":\"2025-06-18T00:00:00.000Z\",\"dateModified\":\"2025-06-18T00:00:00.000Z\"}"}}],[